  "_readme": [
    "Keys that must stay in English in every locale bundle, because the string",
    "IS the thing being taught. Translating them does not localize the lesson,",
    "it breaks it: 'Fan' is only an answer to \"which word rhymes with 'can'?\"",
    "in English, and 'Break a leg' is only an idiom in English.",
    "",
    "check_i18n.py counts these as done rather than pending, so nobody clears",
    "a translation backlog by making the exercises wrong.",
    "",
    "This is a workaround, not a curriculum answer. A Swahili-speaking child",
    "currently gets a translated instruction wrapped around English answers.",
    "The real fix is either Swahili/French phonics of their own for these",
    "lessons, or marking the lesson itself as English-language-instruction so",
    "it can be labelled or skipped. See docs/CONTENT_WORKLIST.md."
  ],
